/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  thermoPhysPropDict (v2) -- phi-phi SRK: one cubic for both phases
  (K_i = phi_L,i / phi_V,i at the two roots), the standard treatment of a
  light-hydrocarbon column at pressure.

  WHY phi-phi (C256, 2026-11-09).  The column runs at 16 bar and its lower
  half sits above the critical temperature of propane (369.8 K): the C4
  side draw leaves stage 13 at about 377 K carrying about 6 % propane, and
  the C5 draw at 423 K is at butane's (425.1 K).  On the gamma-phi package
  (ideal liquid, SRK vapour; C239) that liquid's propane was priced
  through a vapour pressure continued above Tc, where no saturated state
  exists -- a K a student read off the draw that was not a K.  On one
  cubic the liquid fugacity is the EoS's own, defined above any component's
  Tc.  kij = 0 for every pair, announced: the catalogue carries no SRK pair
  for these alkanes, so the answer is the undressed cubic's, not one fitted
  to measured equilibria.  The vapour departure that C239
  measured (phi of the light key about 21 % below 1) is kept: it is the
  same SRK.

  No interior seed is declared (since 2026-11-08, DEV.md 4c C245 slice 4).
  Until then the column started from a stage profile declared in 0/,
  because from the built-in linear start the CMO phase that seeds the full
  MESH converged (|F| 2.6e-14) to a TRIVIAL profile: T 287-300 K, x = y on
  every stage.  A stage vapour at 287 K and 16 bar has ONE cubic root, a
  liquid-like one, and SRK handed it to the vapour too: both phases on one
  root, every K about 1.  The cubic now returns a flagged PSEUDO-ROOT for a
  phase that has no root of its own (CubicEoS.H), and from the linear
  start the CMO phase converges in 14 Newton iterations to the real
  profile and the full MESH in 4 -- the same answer the seed gave.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

recordType    thermophysicalPropertySystem;
schemaVersion 2;

components       ( propane  nButane  nPentane  nHexane );

equilibrium
{
    formulation phiPhi;

    equationOfState
    {
        model      SRK;
        mixingRule vanDerWaalsOneFluid;
    }

    liquid { fugacityRoute equationOfState; root liquid; }
    vapour { fugacityRoute equationOfState; root vapour; }
}

caloric
{
    energyBasis elementsDatum;
    liquid { departureRoute equilibriumEquationOfState; root liquid; }
    vapour { departureRoute equilibriumEquationOfState; root vapour; }
}
